<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIA-TELECOMS-Investors ready for floats.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIA-TELECOMS-Investors ready for floats.</headline>
<byline>Kevin Morrison</byline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Planned floats of Australian telecommunication carriers over the next couple of years are likely to be well received by investors and possibly become the largest industry sector on the local bourse, analysts said.</p>
<p>Optus Communications Pty Ltd is is expected to raise up to A$1.5 billion in a share market float by the end of 1996.</p>
<p>The Australian government is expected to raise an estimated A$8.0 billion from the sale of a third of local telecom giant Telstra Corp in the 1997/98 year. A few other telecom related float are also expected to occur over the next five years.</p>
</text>
